	(text "The tool's 5 V runs over the toolchanger's existing\nwires, its ID in the CAT6 (sheet Toolhead). On only when the\nhost says so (key locked, ID says \"power me\"); off\nat once, locally, when the ID line opens. Its slide\nswitch at OFF (else always on). ON > ~1 V = on: R959\nholds it off through a reset; R960: 1k across supplies."
